{"name":"Meteor Shower","hex":"#5533ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"meteor shower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A phenomenon occurring when many meteors are seen on Earth during a short period of time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meteor_shower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Meteor shower","blocks":[{"text":"A meteor shower is a celestial event in which a number of meteors are observed to radiate, or originate, from one point in the night sky. These meteors are caused by streams of cosmic debris called meteoroids entering Earth's atmosphere at extremely high speeds on parallel trajectories. Most meteors are smaller than a grain of sand, so almost all of them disintegrate and never hit the Earth's surface. Very intense or unusual meteor showers are known as meteor outbursts and meteor storms, which produce at least 1,000 meteors an hour, most notably from the Leonids. The Meteor Data Centre lists over 900 suspected meteor showers of which about 100 are well established. Several organizations point to viewing opportunities on the Internet. NASA maintains a daily map of active meteor showers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Meteor_shower_in_the_Chilean_Desert_%28annotated%29_%28potw2227b%29.jpg/330px-Meteor_shower_in_the_Chilean_Desert_%28annotated%29_%28potw2227b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteor_shower","wikidata":"Q105000"},{"title":"Meteor Shower (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Meteor Shower is a 2009 Chinese television series starring Hans Zhang, Yu Haoming, Vision Wei and Zhu Zixiao. It premiered on Hunan Television on August 8, 2009. It is an unlicensed live-television drama production based on Boys Over Flowers not authorized by Japanese publisher Shueisha. According to the producer, the series is only inspired by the manga and not based on it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Meteor_Shower_TV_series_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteor_Shower_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q5368891"},{"title":"Meteor","blocks":[{"text":"A meteor, known colloquially as a shooting star, is a glowing streak of a small body going through Earth's atmosphere, after being heated to incandescence by collisions with air molecules in the upper atmosphere, creating a streak of light via its rapid motion and sometimes also by shedding glowing material in its wake. Meteors typically occur in the mesosphere at altitudes from 76–100 kilometres. The root word meteor comes from the Greek μετεωρίτης (meteōrítēs), meaning \"high in the air\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Cosmic_Fireball_Falling_Over_ALMA.jpg/330px-Cosmic_Fireball_Falling_Over_ALMA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteor","wikidata":"Q131136"},{"title":"Shower","blocks":[{"text":"A shower is a place in which a person bathes under a spray of typically warm or hot water. Indoors, there is a drain in the floor. Most showers are set up to have adjustable temperature, spray pressure, and showerhead nozzle angle. The simplest showers have a swivelling nozzle aimed downward, while more complex showers have a showerhead connected to a hose that has a mounting bracket; this allows the showerer to hold the showerhead by hand to spray the water onto different parts of their body. A showerhead can be installed in a small shower stall or bathtub, with a plastic shower curtain or door."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Dusche-cut-w025-h025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shower","wikidata":"Q7863"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/PSM_V01_D405_August_meteor_shower_orbit.jpg/500px-PSM_V01_D405_August_meteor_shower_orbit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/PSM_V01_D405_August_meteor_shower_orbit.jpg/500px-PSM_V01_D405_August_meteor_shower_orbit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diagram from 1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APSM_V01_D405_August_meteor_shower_orbit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg/500px-PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg/1280px-PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg/500px-PSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meteor shower on chart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APSM_V18_D201_Shower_of_perseids_sept_6_and_7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Ssc2005-04a_medium.jpg/500px-Ssc2005-04a_medium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Ssc2005-04a_medium.jpg/500px-Ssc2005-04a_medium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comet Encke's meteoroid trail is the diagonal red glow.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASsc2005-04a_medium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Sig06-011_medium.jpg/500px-Sig06-011_medium.jpg?utm_source=e